cording to the given rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =2-3y+z \\\\  & =2-3\\cdot 0+0 \\\\  & =2 \\\\ {z}^{′} & =x+2y \\\\  & =0+2\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =0 \\\\ {w}^{′} & =y-2w \\\\  & =0-2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we add these to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ | $w$ | ${w}^{′}$ | $Δw$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $0$ | $2$ |  | $0$ | $0$ |  | $1$ | $-2$ |  |\n\nFinally, we compute $Δy,$ $Δz,$ and $Δw$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ Δz & ={z}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =0\\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =0 \\\\ Δw & ={w}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add these to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ | $w$ | ${w}^{′}$ | $Δw$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $0$ | $2$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $0$ | $0$ | $0$ | $1$ | $-2$ | $-\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n\nTo get the new values of $x,$ $y,$ $z,$ and $w$ in the *next* row, we add $Δx$ to $x,$ $Δy$ to $y,$ $Δz$ to $z,$ and $Δw$ to $w,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=0+\\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy=0+\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {z}_{\\text{new}} & =z+Δz=0+0=0 \\\\ {w}_{\\text{new}} & =w+Δw=1+\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding these values to our table in a new row gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ | $w$ | ${w}^{′}$ | $Δw$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $0$ | $2$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $0$ | $0$ | $0$ | $1$ | $-2$ | $-\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n| $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |  |  | $0$ |  |  | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |  |  |\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n$$\n\\displaystyle y\\,\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)≈\\frac{1}{2},\n$$\n$z\\,\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)≈0,$