ght)]=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\n$$\n\n- $$\n\\displaystyle {lim}_{x\\to \\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{6}\\right)]=\\frac{\\pi }{2}\n$$\n\n![](images/fa/fa90489ad28c3fde493a83b61ef040867d575ad06c989439de9764d0d23b002e.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2\\sqrt{3}}^{\\infty }\\frac{18}{36+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t & =3\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{a}{6}\\right)]-\\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139539078 17592186576411 true] [17592186616971 1074 "First, let's recall the following result:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{{k}^{2}+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{k}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{k}\\right)+C\n$$\n\nWe proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2\\sqrt{3}}^{\\infty }\\frac{18}{36+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t & =18\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{2\\sqrt{3}}^{a}\\frac{1}{36+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =18\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{2\\sqrt{3}}^{a}\\frac{1}{{6}^{2}+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =18\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{t}{6}\\right)]}_{2\\sqrt{3}}^{a} \\\\  & =3\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{a}{6}\\right)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\right)) \\\\  & =3\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{a}{6}\\right)-\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =3\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{a}{6}\\right)]-\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{6}\\right),$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{6}\\right)]=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }[\\ope